        "Look for:\n- Review count and rating.\n- Recent review activity (“review velocity”).\n- Number of technicians, crews, branches, or service vehicles where visible.\n- Range of services.\n- Signs of active advertising.\n- Website quality and conversion paths.\n- Evidence of meaningful local presence.\n- Publicly available revenue or scale indicators, if reliable.\nDo not present guessed revenue as fact. Public estimates can be inaccurate. Use them as clues, not verified financial statements.",
