        "Best,\n[Your name]\nOutreach rules\n- Personalise the message with an actual observation.\n- Keep it short.\n- Do not claim that the business is losing a specific amount unless you have data.\n- Do not use fake urgency.\n- Do not attach a giant generic audit.\n- Do not demand a call as the first step.\n- Respect opt-outs and applicable marketing laws.\n- Keep a record of contact and follow-up.\n16. The first conversation\nIf the owner replies, do not immediately pitch a full rebuild. Understand the business first.",
        "Questions to ask:\n1. Which services are most valuable or strategically important?\n2. Which services are you trying to grow?\n3. Where do most enquiries currently come from?\n4. Are you running paid campaigns now?\n5. What happens after someone calls or submits a form?\n6. How quickly are new leads contacted?\n7. Which enquiries become booked jobs?\n8. Which jobs are most profitable or best suited to your team?\n9. Do you have capacity to take on more work?\n10. What does a qualified lead mean to your business?\n11. What tracking or reporting do you already trust?\n12. What would make this project worthwhile?\nListen for operational constraints. More leads are not always better if the company cannot answer calls, has no available technicians, or is already at capacity."
