        "24. Niche definition worksheet\nTrade:\nGeography:\nIdeal company size:\nHighest-value services:\nTypical customer problem:\nUrgency of demand:\nHow customers search:\nCommon acquisition channels:\nEvidence of existing ad spend:\nCommon website weaknesses:\nOperational constraints:\nRegulatory or compliance issues:\nWhy this market is attractive:\nWhat I still need to validate:\n25. Prospect scoring worksheet\nScore each item 1–5 and note the evidence.\n| Item | Score | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Established business |  |  |\n| Strong review profile |  |  |\n| Recent review activity |  |  |\n| Multiple services or technicians |  |  |\n| Active advertising evidence |  |  |\n| High-value service line |  |  |\n| Visible conversion leak |  |  |\n| Owner or decision-maker identifiable |  |  |\n| Capacity to handle more jobs |  |  |\n| Contact route available |  |  |\n| Total |  |  |",
        "A high score does not prove willingness to buy. It helps decide which business deserves deeper research.\n26. Conversion audit worksheet\nBusiness:\nService page / campaign:\nDate reviewed:\nAd or search promise:\nLanding-page headline:\nDoes the page match the promise?\nTrust elements present:\nPrimary call to action:\nMobile booking experience:\nForm fields and friction:\nOffer and pricing clarity:\nFollow-up process (known / unknown):\nMain observed leak:\nEvidence:\nRecommended change:\nMetric to monitor:\nQuestions for the owner:\n27. Discovery-call notes\nBusiness goals:\nPriority services:\nCurrent lead sources:\nCurrent ad spend (if disclosed):\nLead volume:\nLead qualification process:\nBooking rate:\nCompleted-job rate:\nAverage job value / contribution (if available):\nCapacity constraints:\nCurrent website / CRM / tracking:\nMain frustration:\nDesired outcome:\nDecision-maker:\nNext step:\n28. Proposal outline\nObjective\nState the business outcome in plain language.\nCurrent situation\nSummarise only verified observations and client-provided information.\nRecommended work\nExplain the funnel or conversion improvements.\nDeliverables\nList each page, integration, workflow, report, and revision included.\nMeasurement\nDefine the metrics and baseline.\nTimeline\nSet milestones and client approval dates.\nInvestment\nSeparate setup fee, recurring fee, and third-party costs.\nClient responsibilities\nList access, content, approvals, lead handling, and data required.\nExclusions\nClarify what is not included.\nAssumptions and limitations\nState dependencies, attribution limits, and factors outside your control.\n29. Launch QA checklist\n- [ ] Client approved all copy and claims.\n- [ ] Correct service, location, phone, and hours.\n- [ ] Price and offer conditions verified.\n- [ ] Reviews and credentials are authentic.\n- [ ] Desktop layout tested.\n- [ ] Mobile layout tested.\n- [ ] All links and buttons tested.\n- [ ] Phone action tested.\n- [ ] Form submission tested.\n- [ ] Notifications reach the correct team.\n- [ ] Confirmation message is accurate.\n- [ ] Analytics events tested.\n- [ ] Privacy notice and consent requirements reviewed.\n- [ ] Lead ownership and response process agreed.\n- [ ] Backup or rollback plan exists.\n- [ ] Client launch approval recorded.\n30. Monthly review worksheet\nReporting period:\nTraffic:\nCalls:\nForms:\nQualified leads:\nBooked jobs:\nCompleted jobs:\nCost per lead:\nCost per booked job:\nRevenue / gross contribution (if known):\nTests completed:\nWhat improved:\nWhat declined:\nData limitations:\nClient feedback:\nNext three actions:"
